+# Bun migration
+
+Use Bun 1.4.4 (the supplied and validated version). Install development dependencies
+with `bun install --frozen-lockfile`.
+
+## Entry points
+
+- `bun run run [name] [count]` runs the CLI.
+- `bash scripts/run.sh [name] [count]` preserves the shell launcher, including
+  invocation from another working directory.
+- `bun run typecheck` performs strict static checking with Bun's native `bun check`
+  and the project tsconfig. `bun run check` and `make check` retain the existing
+  check entry points. CI installs the locked dependencies and runs this check.
+
+The original project had no test, serve, or build task. No such task was added.
+The import alias `@lib/` now lives in `tsconfig.json`. The source shebang invokes
+Bun with automatic environment-file loading disabled. Deno configuration and
+execution have been removed.
+
+## Behavior and security
+
+Arguments, defaults, trimming, JSON output, positive-integer validation, error
+text, and exit status 2 for invalid counts are preserved. Environment reads use
+`process.env`; absent values still produce JSON null.
+
+Bun normally loads environment files automatically. `bunfig.toml` sets
+`env = false` so `bun run run` and direct project invocations read inherited
+variables only, matching the original behavior. The source shebang and shell
+launcher additionally use `--no-env-file`. Explicit `--env-file` remains an
+opt-in Bun feature. See the [Bun environment documentation](https://bun.com/docs/runtime/environment-variables).
+
+Bun does not enforce Deno's runtime permission boundary. The old launcher granted
+all environment access but restricted filesystem, network, subprocess, and other
+capabilities by default. The Bun process has the operating-system permissions of
+its user. Run it in an external sandbox/container if that isolation is required.
+The application itself still only reads arguments and two environment variables.
+
+There were no external application dependencies to preserve. The only added
+direct development dependency is exact-pinned `@types/node` 26.6.5 for the
+Node-compatible `process` API; `bun.lock` pins its transitive dependency too.
+Bun 1.4.4 supplies the checker, so no TypeScript compiler package is needed.
+Formatting and lint replacement were outside this migration's scope.
+
+## Validation
+
+- Captured the original Deno default and named-argument output and strict check.
+- `bun install --frozen-lockfile` succeeded using the local installation cache.
+- `bun run typecheck` and `make check` passed.
+- 35 automated assertions covered default/custom/empty names, invalid counts,
+  inherited versus dotenv environment variables, the package/direct/shell entry
+  points, shell invocation from outside the project, and rejection of an injected
+  type error. The injected error and temporary environment file were removed.
+- Verified no Deno execution/configuration references remain in project code.
+
+The hosted GitHub Actions workflow was updated but was not executed remotely.
